Output is routed to run.log rather than discarded, so hiding noise never loses information needed to debug a run; that is why quiet() redirects to the log and the warnings hook writes known messages there instead of using warnings.filterwarnings (filtered warnings vanish entirely). Warnings are matched by message, not module or category, so new warnings from the same libraries still show. Logger handling has two traps found on a real run: WhisperX installs its own stdout handler on first get_logger() unless the 'whisperx' logger already has a handler, so setup adds one first; Lightning adds a console handler to 'lightning.pytorch' when imported (after setup, since stage modules import lazily), so configuring that parent had no effect and the migration-utils child logger that emits the checkpoint-upgrade message is configured with propagate=False instead. The Tee skips chunks containing \r so tqdm redraws don't flood the log. Demucs' own progress bar restarts per model in a bag; a callback-driven single bar computes the chunk total from Separator's private _segment/_overlap/_shifts, with a fallback to a counting bar if those ever change.
